            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Malayalam for to say goodbye, then the Malayalam for to leave one's homeland."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ശവസംസ്കാരം",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ശവസംസ്കാരം — śavasaṁskāraṁ — \"a funeral\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "മുത്തച്ഛന്റെ ശവസംസ്കാരം ഇന്നലെ വൈകുന്നേരം നടന്നു. muttacchanṟe śavasaṁskāraṁ innale vaikunnēraṁ naṭannu. Grandfather's funeral took place yesterday evening."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ശവം, a body, + സംസ്കാരം, rites: the last rites."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ശവസംസ്കാരം (śavasaṁskāraṁ) is built from two Sanskrit words, śava, \"a corpse\" (CDIAL 12356), and saṁskāra, \"preparation, a rite\" (CDIAL 13038), which also gave സംസ്കാരം (saṁskāraṁ), \"culture\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
        },
